RustyUI local changes to libtermkey 0.22
======================================

Reference: https://github.com/deepin-community/libtermkey/
Compared against commit 2fedbe4081a03104ab95d58719345e1ba85d341f.
The exact historical import commit is not known. Comparison ignored comments,
whitespace, added statement braces and preprocessor line continuations; this
was a source-token review, not a proof of semantic equivalence.

Existing differences before vendoring:
* All five files: RustyAxe include paths, copyright headers and formatting
  (including added statement braces); upstream MIT notice now restored.
* termkey.h: upstream C++ extern "C" guards absent in the local header.
* termkey-internal.h: no other token differences found.
* termkey.c: signed %i instead of %u for mouse coordinates (int arguments);
  add missing break after TERMKEY_TYPE_MODEREPORT formatting.
* driver-csi.c: correct debug format for size_t args (%zu); local replacement
  of strncpy with strlcpy in saved OSC/DCS strings was incorrect (truncation
  and possible read beyond the bounded terminal input).
* driver-ti.c: check insert_seq result and free the unused node on failure.

Vendor relocation:
* Restore upstream filenames and local header includes; remove RustyAxe/UI
  umbrella includes and add direct standard-library includes.
* driver-csi.c: use bounded memcpy for exactly len payload bytes followed
  by NUL; check allocation failure before copying.
* driver-ti.c: check node allocation before insertion.
* Keep termkey.h installed under librustyui for existing native consumers;
  the implementation remains bundled, using system terminfo.
* Exclude vendor directories from automated source formatting.

Do not run project-wide header or formatting rewrites on these files.
Keep upstream licensing and document subsequent local patches here.
